# execution_order API — NestJS request lifecycle demo
# The demo is the SERVER CONSOLE LOG sequence, not the HTTP response:
#   middleware -> guard -> interceptor(before) -> pipes -> controller -> service
#   -> interceptor(after). POST / triggers the full pipeline (guard/interceptor/
#   pipe are route-level); GET / runs only middleware + the global ValidationPipe.

### 1. Hello — GET / runs middleware + global pipe only
GET http://localhost:3000

### 2. POST — full pipeline: guard + interceptor + MyPipe + global ValidationPipe.
###    Watch the console for the ordered logs. Body is validated by the DTO
###    (name/age/email); the extra "url" field is stripped by whitelist: true.
POST http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Apache",
  "age": 12,
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "url": "http://localhost:3000"
}

### 3. POST — invalid body: age is a string, so ValidationPipe rejects (400)
POST http://localhost:3000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Apache",
  "age": "twelve",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com"
}
